  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-08-31T04:35:58.189Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This is similar to \"Appear Offline\" request ( http://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/add-a-stealth-mode-to-allow-people-to-appear-offline ), but instead of hiding whole user presence in the app, this feature should only hide the instance where user currently in. So, other friends-users will see that the user is online and available for communication, but they not able to see world and instance the user in. Friends should able to do join requests as if the user in private instance. In short, this feature should simulate \" being in private instance\" appearance in social menu. \n\nThis feature can prevent unwanted friend joins (especially \"friends of friends of friends of ...\" waves) and spying, but should signal friends that you actually online and able to communicate. It's should be useful for socially active users who have a lot of friends from a lots of different social groups, who want to keep them isolated and avoid unwanted spontaneous interference.",
